 TR-2  Ciphertext Integrity Test                                   [aes-gcm]
==============================================================================
  Objective : Demonstrate that modification of the protected application record by the malicious actor causes authentication verification to fail and the record to be rejected.
  Procedure :
              1. Sender protects an application record.
              2. Malicious actor intercepts it in flight and flips one ciphertext bit.
              3. Only the modified record is delivered to the receiver.
              4. Repeat for every bit of an 8-byte record (exhaustive sweep).
  Input     : A valid protected record with exactly one ciphertext bit inverted.
  Expected  : AUTH_FAILED; no application record is released.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  > Single-bit modification of the ciphertext
      original protected record (102 bytes = 40 header + 46 ciphertext + 16 tag)
